  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the source-room instructions and raw files first, then build a reproducible analysis pipeline and use its outputs consistently in the workbook, report, slides, and metrics JSON. I’ll verify the arithmetic and render the documents before wrapping up.",
    "The source room is reachable and lists the expected raw exports, corrections, costing assumptions, archived ECB/WB data, and metadata. I’m saving those files locally before analysis so the calculations and provenance register are reproducible from the frozen inputs.",
    "The accounting rules call for revision selection before eligibility filters, and for returns to be joined only after both revision resolution and shipment eligibility. I’m encoding those steps explicitly in the analysis so duplicates, superseded rows, out-of-window returns, and orphan links remain visible in the quality record.",
    "The initial reconciliation is clean: 1,254 eligible shipments across 72 country-month cells, with monthly totals matching country totals and all order-level contribution identities passing. The leading feasible pair is CZE + ESP under base and stress, but the source room has no real catchment, lead-time, or hub-cost observations, so I’m making the recommendation explicitly stage-gated.",
    "A final content check caught one important wording error: the recommended Czechia + Spain case is exposed to the modeled CZK haircut. I’m correcting the report and slide to show the FX stress accurately before the final rebuild.",
    "The rendered report exposed a sign error in the alternative-comparison sentence: the selected case was correctly ahead, but the prose displayed the difference as negative. I’m fixing that comparison and rerunning the checks.",
    "## Deliverables\n\n- [Executive report](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_executive_report.pdf>)\n- [Board presentation](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_board_presentation.pdf>)\n- [Analytical workbook](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/Meridian_Analysis.xlsx>)\n- [Metrics JSON](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json>)\n- [Source register](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/source_register.csv>) · [Reproduction guide](<<CELL>/workspace/README.md>) · [Verification results](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/verification.json>) · [Saved raw source register](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/source-room/source-register.json>)\n\nThe model favors a **staged Czechia + Spain case**: €225,000 capex, 5 FTE, €198,099 base annual incremental contribution after recurring fixed costs, €32,180 under the defined stress, and 1.14-year simple base payback. This is scenario arithmetic on synthetic client data, so the report gates irreversible spending on validating the assumed uplift and savings with actual operating evidence.\n\n**Verification:** 517 checks passed with none failing. The 8-page report and 6-page presentation were rendered for visual review; the 13-sheet workbook was checked against the metrics and scenario calculations. Reconciliation and exception handling are recorded in the deliverables, including duplicate rows, revisions, excluded orders, valid zero-price shipments, a late return, and a quarantined orphan return."
  ],
  "final": "## Deliverables\n\n- [Executive report](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_executive_report.pdf>)\n- [Board presentation](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_board_presentation.pdf>)\n- [Analytical workbook](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/Meridian_Analysis.xlsx>)\n- [Metrics JSON](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json>)\n- [Source register](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/source_register.csv>) · [Reproduction guide](<<CELL>/workspace/README.md>) · [Verification results](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/verification.json>) · [Saved raw source register](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/source-room/source-register.json>)\n\nThe model favors a **staged Czechia + Spain case**: €225,000 capex, 5 FTE, €198,099 base annual incremental contribution after recurring fixed costs, €32,180 under the defined stress, and 1.14-year simple base payback. This is scenario arithmetic on synthetic client data, so the report gates irreversible spending on validating the assumed uplift and savings with actual operating evidence.\n\n**Verification:** 517 checks passed with none failing. The 8-page report and 6-page presentation were rendered for visual review; the 13-sheet workbook was checked against the metrics and scenario calculations. Reconciliation and exception handling are recorded in the deliverables, including duplicate rows, revisions, excluded orders, valid zero-price shipments, a late return, and a quarantined orphan return.",
